> It's the old noun-verb problem: {la teris po'u lo tirxu} doesn't actually
> add any real information that {la teris noi tirxu} doesn't. This comes up
> again and again: Lojban really "wants" to be verby, English is innately
> very nouny, and as English speakers use Lojban, it seems to get
> progressively nounier and nounier.
>
> mi'e la latro'a mu'o
>
